<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brenz (river)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Brenz is a river in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> that rises in the Brenztopf spring at Königsbronn on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabian-jura">Swabian Jura</a> and flows south past Heidenheim and Giengen to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near Lauingen. Its valley has been an industrial area since early modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-technology">ironworking</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brenz-river.jpg" alt="Brenz (river)" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ssch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brenztopf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
